# Preview tunnel authority (founder mobile review)

The public cloud preview tunnel is **not** whatever branch happens to be checked out on a random agent VM.

## Git source (mandatory)

| Ref | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **`preview/tunnel`** | Branch the tunnel worktree mounts (`origin/preview/tunnel`). Fast-forwarded from **`main`** after every merge (GitHub Action + `sync-preview-tunnel-branch.sh`). |
| **`main`** | Production source of truth; all agent PRs merge here in-session. |
| **`cursor/*` feature branches** | **Not founder-visible** on the tunnel until merged to `main` (then `preview/tunnel` updates). |

Serve preview with **`serve-site00-preview-from-main.sh`** (name legacy; tracks **`preview/tunnel`**). Do **not** use `ensure-grok-environment-unified-preview.sh` for founder workspace review unless explicitly reviewing that Grok branch.

## Cloud agent shipping (all models — Composer, Opus, etc.)

1. Branch from **`main`**, PR to **`main`**, **merge in the same session** (unless founder says draft / wait).
2. After merge, run **`bash .cursor/scripts/post-merge-preview-tunnel-refresh.sh`** on the **canonical preview environment** when you have pushed to `origin/main` (CI also syncs `preview/tunnel` on push to `main`).
3. Do not leave founder-facing work only on a long-lived `cursor/*` branch.

## Tunnel connector (mandatory)

- Only the environment with **`SITE00_CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_CANONICAL=1`** in Cursor Cloud Secrets may run `cloudflared`.
- All other agents: tunnel script exits without registering a connector.
- Docs: `docs/site00/production-workspace/reconciliation/preview-tunnel-multi-connector-2026-10-06.md`

## Verify

- `/tmp/site00-preview-runtime-lineage.txt` → `PREVIEW_AUTHORITY=origin/preview/tunnel` and SHA matches latest merged `main`.
- Page source on tunnel: `/src/main.tsx?v=dev-local` (dev mode), not stale unrelated `index.*.js` from another connector.
